    "changelog_excerpt": "# 🚀 DMTools Release v1.7.277\n\n## 📝 What's Changed\n\nFull diff: [v1.7.276...v1.7.277](https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/compare/v1.7.276...v1.7.277)\n\n### 🚀 Features\n- Env_get / env_list - non-secret configuration for JS agents, one policy (JsEnvPolicy) (731bbd1c)\n\n### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n- Confluence with CONFLUENCE_LOGIN_PASS_TOKEN is reported as configured (#712) (f8f3fb53)\n- Dmtools upgrade works on installs that still have the old wrapper (#701) (47ffe955)\n- Jira-style field names are mapped to ADO reference names (agents#880) (c4bf3501)\n- Silence the harmless GraalVM TruffleAttach warning on every JS-agent run (#697) (42d7687a)\n- WIQL link queries (FROM WorkItemLinks) return their work items (agents#871) (798214d7)\n\n### 📦 Dependencies\n- Auth (#706) (c4316a60)\n- Aws-core (#704) (56c68b67)\n- Aws-core (#717) (52611251)\n- Bump gradle-wrapper from 9.8.0 to 9.8.1 (#705) (b8ee9a07)\n- Ignore jtoon 2.0.6+ in dependabot and move to 2.0.5 (Java 17 baseline) (82cc58fd)\n- Regions (#702) (95105d7b)\n\n### 🛠 Maintenance\n- Bump submodule — ADO fixes (#870, #873, #874, #877, #878, #881, #882), auto-save template (#883), project resolution (1529a8ea)\n- Update coverage badge (#711) (52ec683e)\n\n---\n\nThis release includes the **DMTools CLI** and **Agent Skill** for enterprise dark-factory orchestration across MCP tools, AI agents, and delivery workflows.\n\n## 📦 What's Included\n\n### 🖥️ DMTools CLI\n- **Command-line interface** for DMTools operations\n- **Java-based** automation and integration tools\n- **Cross-platform install scripts** for easy setup (`install`, `install.sh`, `install.bat`, `install.ps1`)\n- **Wrapper script** (`dmtools.sh`)\n\n### 🤖 DMTools Agent Skill\n- **AI assistant skill** for MCP, AI agents, and generative-ai-friendly DMTools workflows in Cursor, Claude, Codex, and other Agent Skills compatible systems\n- **Complete DMtools documentation** (67+ MCP tools, JavaScript agent development, and configuration guides)\n- **Cross-platform support** (works with all major AI coding assistant..."
